<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA'S AIR CONTROLLERS STAGE ONE HOUR STRIKE.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA'S AIR CONTROLLERS STAGE ONE HOUR STRIKE.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's air controllers said they would close for an hour the Sofia airport on Tuesday as part of nationwide strikes and protests against forming a second socialist cabinet and for immediate general elections.</p>
<p>&quot;Aircraft will not land and take off from 3 p.m. until 4 p.m.,&quot; a senior air controller said.</p>
<p>On Monday the air contollers also held an hour strike but it did not cause major disturbances in the schedule, airport officials said.</p>
<p>-- Galina Sabeva, Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
</text>
